WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.667
(bomb explodes)

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:18.940
- [Evan] How to delight customers.

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:21.733
My goal is to delight my
own family of customers.

00:00:21.733 --> 00:00:23.611
Just like my dad did for his.

00:00:23.611 --> 00:00:24.550
Louis Trahan,

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:26.260
Founder of Last Minute Training.

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:27.330
(light music)

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:28.672
Louis Trahan had a problem,

00:00:28.672 --> 00:00:31.124
he's in a boring industry.

00:00:31.124 --> 00:00:32.091
Louis' company,

00:00:32.091 --> 00:00:32.924
Last Minute Training

00:00:32.924 --> 00:00:35.302
sells training for office workers.

00:00:35.302 --> 00:00:37.493
Most people don't think about
training until they need it

00:00:37.493 --> 00:00:39.826
and it's really hard to get people excited

00:00:39.826 --> 00:00:41.026
and talking about it.

00:00:41.026 --> 00:00:43.509
Most people see training
as a necessary evil,

00:00:43.509 --> 00:00:45.482
not something to look forward to.

00:00:45.482 --> 00:00:48.078
When was the last time you
went around telling everyone

00:00:48.078 --> 00:00:50.361
you know about that amazing Excel training

00:00:50.361 --> 00:00:52.765
you just can't wait to take?

00:00:52.765 --> 00:00:53.598
Exactly.

00:00:54.447 --> 00:00:55.280
But with my help,

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:57.800
Louis realized that he
doesn't really sell training,

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:00.900
he sells the experience
of being delighted.

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:02.340
His one word is delight

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.107
and he built his entire
business around it.

00:01:05.107 --> 00:01:08.816
He delights his customers by
actually caring about them.

00:01:08.816 --> 00:01:09.649
He and his team research

00:01:09.649 --> 00:01:12.111
and know more about all the
training options available

00:01:12.111 --> 00:01:13.578
than any other competitor,

00:01:13.578 --> 00:01:16.957
so he can give the best
recommendations to his clients.

00:01:16.957 --> 00:01:18.268
He knows which training providers

00:01:18.268 --> 00:01:21.353
deliver the highest quality
training for each subject area,

00:01:21.353 --> 00:01:23.529
who is least likely to cancel classes

00:01:23.529 --> 00:01:27.398
and who has the best learning
environment for his customers.

00:01:27.398 --> 00:01:28.795
He often books people into courses

00:01:28.795 --> 00:01:30.477
where he makes less money

00:01:30.477 --> 00:01:34.322
because it's the right
thing for the client.

00:01:34.322 --> 00:01:35.795
When he interviews new staff members,

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:37.954
he first looks at whether
they have an attitude

00:01:37.954 --> 00:01:39.196
of delighting people,

00:01:39.196 --> 00:01:41.176
before he looks at their skills,

00:01:41.176 --> 00:01:42.009
experience,

00:01:42.009 --> 00:01:43.071
or references.

00:01:43.071 --> 00:01:44.208
In his marketing,

00:01:44.208 --> 00:01:46.293
he shows a picture of his baby son smiling

00:01:46.293 --> 00:01:48.640
because he wants people to feel delighted

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:51.006
when they see his ads.

00:01:51.006 --> 00:01:52.020
The results,

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:53.303
when I first me Louis

00:01:53.303 --> 00:01:54.738
and he joined my mastermind group,

00:01:54.738 --> 00:01:57.036
he had just an idea on paper,

00:01:57.036 --> 00:01:58.943
it was a pure startup.

00:01:58.943 --> 00:02:00.104
Fast forward a few years

00:02:00.104 --> 00:02:01.448
and Louis now has an office,

00:02:01.448 --> 00:02:02.281
a team,

00:02:02.281 --> 00:02:03.365
brand name clients,

00:02:03.365 --> 00:02:05.477
sells over 10,000 training classes

00:02:05.477 --> 00:02:09.509
and has booked almost
$10,000,000 in business.

00:02:09.509 --> 00:02:10.600
He's making money

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:11.927
and making an impact.

00:02:11.927 --> 00:02:14.997
So I asked Louis to share
how he found his one word.

00:02:14.997 --> 00:02:17.557
(light piano music)

00:02:17.557 --> 00:02:18.768
It was over 20 years ago

00:02:18.768 --> 00:02:21.162
but I can still remember
it like it was yesterday.

00:02:21.162 --> 00:02:22.566
I woke up on Christmas morning,

00:02:22.566 --> 00:02:24.409
wondering where dad was.

00:02:24.409 --> 00:02:26.786
He was gone because it was cold outside.

00:02:26.786 --> 00:02:28.025
I mean really cold,

00:02:28.025 --> 00:02:29.267
like 50 below.

00:02:29.267 --> 00:02:30.938
And another family needed him

00:02:30.938 --> 00:02:32.370
to come fix their broken furnace.

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:33.788
(light music)

00:02:33.788 --> 00:02:34.852
He was a furnace repairman

00:02:34.852 --> 00:02:36.369
and these were his customers.

00:02:36.369 --> 00:02:39.386
Dad always went above and
beyond to help a customer,

00:02:39.386 --> 00:02:41.248
even if they were total strangers,

00:02:41.248 --> 00:02:44.076
especially on Christmas.

00:02:44.076 --> 00:02:46.962
This wasn't the first or
last holiday without him.

00:02:46.962 --> 00:02:50.590
Dad hated seeing people suffering.

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:52.167
I could tell you story after story

00:02:52.167 --> 00:02:54.310
where he aimed to bring joy and relief

00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:56.877
to the people around him in every moment,

00:02:56.877 --> 00:02:59.646
often at his own expense or his family's,

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:01.185
and now I understand.

00:03:01.185 --> 00:03:03.458
We were all family to him.

00:03:03.458 --> 00:03:04.729
Every person.

00:03:04.729 --> 00:03:07.730
Now my goal is to delight
my own family of customers,

00:03:07.730 --> 00:03:09.754
just like my dad did for his.

00:03:09.754 --> 00:03:10.707
I can't help it,

00:03:10.707 --> 00:03:11.903
it's ingrained in me,

00:03:11.903 --> 00:03:13.714
it's part of my DNA.

00:03:13.714 --> 00:03:14.887
And let's be honest,

00:03:14.887 --> 00:03:16.437
you probably rarely think

00:03:16.437 --> 00:03:19.546
of scheduling training as
a delightful experience.

00:03:19.546 --> 00:03:20.379
In reality,

00:03:20.379 --> 00:03:21.695
it's probably a huge headache.

00:03:21.695 --> 00:03:22.617
(light music)

00:03:22.617 --> 00:03:24.431
Most of our clients tell
us they would previously

00:03:24.431 --> 00:03:27.086
spend hours and hours researching

00:03:27.086 --> 00:03:30.032
and then booking and
managing multiple vendors

00:03:30.032 --> 00:03:32.569
for a variety of
different training classes

00:03:32.569 --> 00:03:35.870
only to get inadequate
or even canceled classes.

00:03:35.870 --> 00:03:38.902
We screen the vendors
and trainers for quality,

00:03:38.902 --> 00:03:40.559
making sure we understand your needs

00:03:40.559 --> 00:03:41.945
to get you the right training,

00:03:41.945 --> 00:03:44.635
plus we negotiate the deal for you.

00:03:44.635 --> 00:03:46.275
Our staff can often find you

00:03:46.275 --> 00:03:47.931
the right training class in minutes,

00:03:47.931 --> 00:03:50.057
where it might take you
days to complete the search

00:03:50.057 --> 00:03:52.169
for the right class on your own.

00:03:52.169 --> 00:03:55.026
I've built an entire team
made up of people who,

00:03:55.026 --> 00:03:56.127
just like my dad,

00:03:56.127 --> 00:03:59.137
will bend over backwards to delight you.

00:03:59.137 --> 00:04:01.008
It wouldn't matter what
kind of business I'm in,

00:04:01.008 --> 00:04:03.500
my number one priority would still be

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:05.494
to delight my customers.

00:04:05.494 --> 00:04:07.994
(light music)

00:04:27.293 --> 00:04:29.960
(bomb explodes)

